        "--prompt-en",
        "A photographic espionage scene in a closed service room beside a freight railway yard on a rainy midday. The primary subject is a woman. Use the supplied portrait as guidance for her facial appearance and short dark bob. The woman is engaged in espionage work: she watches a cream utility van through the narrow window while assembling a contemporaneous field record. Outside, the van has stopped beside a freight wagon, its red diagonal door marking distinct against the wet concrete. Inside, a long-lens camera rests firmly on a beanbag at the window, its optical axis aimed at that van. Its rear display shows a recently captured view of the same van. An open notebook immediately beside the camera contains a small printed image of that vehicle above fresh rows of pencilled observation marks. Her right forearm rests on the table, the pencil tip meeting the next row in the notebook; her left hand holds a wired radio microphone just below her mouth. The microphone cable visibly descends to a compact radio clipped to her waist. Her gaze remains directed toward the van while her pencil pauses, an attentive, quietly self-possessed presence rather than a posed demonstration. She sits squarely on a wooden stool, both feet on the floor, with her body beside the camera so the long lens has a clear route through the window. A soft charcoal knit collar under a weathered olive jacket, natural lips and a loose bob catching window light give her restrained personal warmth within the concentrated task. Photograph from across the narrow aisle, at seated chest height, with her face in three-quarter view and the table and window visible together. The observer, the notebook evidence, the camera aimed at its subject and the van beyond the glass form a clear continuous triangle. Use a landscape frame and moderate depth of field so her face and hands remain immediate while the van's matching door mark stays recognizable. Daylight enters from the left window, brightening the nearby tabletop and falling to a softer level deeper in the room. Cool diffuse daylight reveals rain streaks on the pane, worn paint and the real scale of the cramped room. The image should feel like an interrupted minute of patient work, with the outside vehicle's pause making this record matter now.",
